		"Students explore a particular period or century through examination of selected literary and non-literary works within their socio-historical and cultural contexts. Coursework includes discussion, analysis and interpretation of representative works. Sample topics: \"19th-Century French Literature,\" \"La Belle Epoque,\" and \"20th-Century French Literature.\" May be repeated if period is different. Taught in French. Prerequisite: minimum of one 250-level course (two recommended). Counts towards medieval studies major."
